From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:20:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: release decoder sessions without prepared buffers

vdec_queue_setup() initializes a firmware session before any compressed
input is queued. With DMABUF queues, vb2 does not call buf_init until
buffer memory is imported, and does not call buf_cleanup for buffers
that were never prepared.

Firmware teardown normally runs from vdec_buf_cleanup() when buf_count
reaches zero. Closing a decoder after REQBUFS, or after STREAMON without
any QBUF, skips that callback and removes the host instance without
ending its firmware session. Repeated empty MediaCodec start/stop cycles
can exhaust firmware sessions and make subsequent REQBUFS fail with EIO
and HFI_ERR_SYS_MAX_SESSIONS_REACHED.

Release a remaining firmware session on close when no prepared buffers
are left. Reuse the normal session-release helper so an empty started
session also stops, unloads its resources and frees internal buffers.
Prepared buffers retain their existing teardown through the m2m context
release; an uninitialized or already released session is not released
again.

Source: local device integration, not an upstream backport.
Base: msm8953-mainline/linux 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429,
with this device's preceding kernel patches applied.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
@@ -1921,6 +1921,11 @@ static int vdec_close(struct file *file)
 	vdec_pm_get(inst);
 	vdec_eos_cancel(inst);
 	cancel_work_sync(&inst->delayed_process_work);
+
+	/* Unprepared DMABUF buffers never reach vdec_buf_cleanup(). */
+	if (!inst->buf_count && inst->state != INST_UNINIT)
+		vdec_session_release(inst);
+
 	venus_close_common(inst, file);
 	ida_destroy(&inst->dpb_ids);
 	vdec_pm_put(inst, false);
-- 
